                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "3D Hardcore Cube 2 is a terrible game.\n\nThe gameplay feels like a prototype or a developer's first game. In every single aspect from gameplay mechanics, to how the game looks and feels. \n\nThe hitboxes feel completely random. For example: I jumped after the obstacle had already moved out of its way (the red cube wall of death) and yet still died to an invisible hitbox for no reason. It feels completely unpolished (and doesn't seem to receive any updates).\n\nMovement is absolutely abysmal.\nDo you want to freeze on nothing randomly?\nJump uncertain of whether the game will actually register the input?\nOR\nOnce again wonder, if the game will calculate the jump to be too low or too high, either over the part you want or straight into the obstacle you were trying to avoid in the first place?\n\nEssentially, jumping feels like RNG, especially on the levels that require you to make precise jumps onto individual cubes. The difficulty spike in levels becomes intolerable, to the point where I began to wonder if the game was just respawning me, and resetting the objects positions I died so much to a few particular red walls.\n\nMost of the levels require you to memorise the paths of objects to avoid them, which is quite tedious. This is not implemented well in my opinion, as there are quite difficult obstacles that require perfect timing, but then you move onto another obstacle that requires you to perfectly time each jump. Should you make a mistake or a poorly timed jump, you are sent STRAIGHT BACK TO THE BEGINNING!\n\nDuring my gameplay I had the intrusive music muted the entire time although this is subjective to taste.\n\nJust avoid unless you're a fan of intrusive music (which I muted the entire time, though that's subjective) and specifically timed mechanics that require you to be precise while you are struggling with poorly programmed controls.",
